refused: d207_spacing_and_checking.cy:7:19, line 7 column 19
 7 |     let $b: i32 = $a+1;
   |                   ^^^^
 fix:  `$a + 1`
 why:  a binary operator, `=` and word operators included, has one space on each side, so `1+8` is refused (D23, D213)

refused: d207_spacing_and_checking.cy:8:19, line 8 column 19
 8 |     let $c: i64 = $a;
   |                   ^^
 what: this is `i32`, where `i64` is needed
 why:  `:` doesn't convert, and `as` builds a new value of another type (D7)
